  "id": "sorbian_folk_music",
  "name": "Serbska ludowa hudźba (Sorbian folk music of Lusatia)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Song and dance music of the Sorbs (Wends), a West Slavic minority of Upper and Lower Lusatia whose cultural centre is Bautzen in eastern Saxony. Village dances were played on the kozoł, a large goatskin bagpipe with a single drone, together with the Sorbian fiddles (husle), while the song repertoire was gathered by Leopold Haupt and Jan Arnošt Smoler in their two-volume Volkslieder der Wenden (1841-43). The cimpoi card stands in for the kozoł, and the fiddle card for the Sorbian fiddles.",
  "recipe": "classic early-1840s serbska ludowa hudźba, drone Modal, wind pipe branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment, single lead single track no stacking. fiddle, cimpoi. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
